---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The compound interest gap — five small explainers"
  description="One slider showing why investing ten years earlier beats investing more money."
  accent="blue"
  activePath={`${base}compound-interest/`}
>
  <h1>Why ten years earlier beats saving more</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Alex starts investing now. Jordan waits ten years, then starts putting
    away the exact same amount every month. Drag the slider forward in time
    and watch what that ten-year head start is actually worth.
  </p>

  <section class="panel" aria-label="Simulation">
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="control">
        <label for="years-slider"
          >Years elapsed <output id="years-output" for="years-slider">25</output></label
        >
        <input type="range" id="years-slider" min="0" max="35" step="1" value="25" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="assumption">
      Both contribute $400 a month at an assumed 7% average annual return —
      the only difference is when they start.
    </p>

    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="value" id="alex-value">—</span>
        <span class="label">Alex — started at year 0</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="value" id="jordan-value">—</span>
        <span class="label">Jordan — started at year 10</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bars" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="bar-col">
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill bar-alex" id="alex-bar"></div></div>
        <span class="bar-caption">Alex</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-col">
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill bar-jordan" id="jordan-bar"></div></div>
        <span class="bar-caption">Jordan</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <svg class="growth-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="chart-title">
      <title id="chart-title">Portfolio value over time for both investors</title>
      <polyline id="jordan-line" class="line-jordan" points="" />
      <polyline id="alex-line" class="line-alex" points="" />
      <line id="year-marker" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="200" class="marker" />
    </svg>
    <p class="chart-legend">
      <span class="swatch swatch-alex"></span>Alex &nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="swatch swatch-jordan"
      ></span>Jordan
    </p>

    <p id="gap-readout" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="explainer">
    <h2>Where the gap actually comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Every dollar you invest keeps earning returns on top of its previous
      returns, so a contribution's value depends far more on how long it's
      been compounding than on its size. Alex's first deposits have an extra
      decade to snowball before Jordan even begins, and that decade sits at
      the most valuable end of the timeline — compounding grows
      multiplicatively, so the years right after money is deposited are
      worth less than the years long after, when the balance itself is
      large. By the time Jordan starts, some of Alex's early contributions
      have already roughly doubled. Jordan can't buy that decade back at any
      contribution size; even doubling or tripling the monthly amount closes
      the gap only slowly, because the missing time was the most productive
      part of the curve. This is the core case for starting small and early
      over waiting to start big.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initCompoundInterest } from "../scripts/compound-interest";
  initCompoundInterest();
</script>

<style>
  .assumption {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .bars {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    height: 14rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bar-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    width: 6rem;
  }

  .bar-track {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    background: #eef0f5;
    border-radius: 0.4rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bar-fill {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 0.4rem 0.4rem 0 0;
    transition: height 0.15s ease;
  }

  .bar-alex {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .bar-jordan {
    background: #9ca3af;
  }

  .bar-caption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .line-alex {
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }

  .line-jordan {
    stroke: #9ca3af;
  }

  .swatch-alex {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .swatch-jordan {
    background: #9ca3af;
  }

  #gap-readout {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (width <= 480px) {
    .bars {
      gap: 1.5rem;
      height: 11rem;
    }
  }
</style>
